         Huge Pages when this is 'advise' or 'always' (forkrun hints for it
         automatically). For the larger throughput gain observed on memfd-backed
         I/O (~50-60% on -s/-b/-C modes, and a large drop in system time, most
         notably in -C mode), 'always' is currently required -- 'advise' does not
         cover plain read/write I/O the way forkrun uses it today. Consider:
           echo always | sudo tee /sys/kernel/mm/transparent_hugepage/shmem_enabled
         or, for the more conservative system-wide setting:
           echo advise | sudo tee /sys/kernel/mm/transparent_hugepage/shmem_enabled
